1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,060
Monday evening, April 15, 1912.

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:05,930
A New Haven paper tells its readers:

3
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:10,017
Titanic afloat. No lives lost.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,790
In New York, crowds push into the

5
00:00:12,830 --> 00:00:16,657
White Star Line's office, waiting for names.

6
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,250
But the ship had sunk before dawn,

7
00:00:19,290 --> 00:00:21,760
hours before that paper was printed.

8
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:23,850
Tuesday morning, the New-York Tribune:

9
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:26,760
1,340 dead.

10
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:30,322
In Oregon, the count is 1,492.

11
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,450
The Carpathia picked up 706 people

12
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:39,384
from the lifeboats.

13
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,554
Everyone else was gone.

14
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,259
No lives lost, the paper said.

15
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,050
The National Archives count:

16
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:50,889
1,517 died.
